    "summary": "Soaring HCS > China > Rider and tight Playin' In The Band with Wall‑of‑Sound clarity",
    "blurb": "The show shines on the Here Comes Sunshine → China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider sequence, featuring Jerry's blistering Strat tone. Playin' In The Band is driven by Phil’s thunderous bass and a rock‑solid rhythm section. Overall performance is high‑energy and captured with excellent soundboard fidelity.",
    "review": "Feb 17 1973 at the St. Paul Auditorium captures the Dead in top form, riding the newly‑installed Wall of Sound to deliver a performance that still feels fresh. The first set builds steadily, but it’s the second‑set highlight—Here Comes Sunshine segued into China Cat Sunflower and then into I Know You Rider—that truly defines the night; Jerry’s soaring leads and Keith’s tasteful piano fills weave a seamless tapestry while Phil’s bass bombs propel the jam forward. Playin' In The Band erupts later with a tight, driving groove anchored by Bill’s steady backbeat and Phil’s muscular low end, culminating in a joyous crescendo that spills into Big River and a rousing encore of Casey Jones. Across all five soundboard sources the mix is crisp, with superb instrument separation that lets every nuance of this high‑energy set shine.",
